"                  ╔══════════════════════════════════════ Help ══════════════════════════════════════╗                  "
"                  ║  About                │ ── Modes ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ▲                  "
"                  ║  Keys ▾               │ - Keys are vim's, in its modes; the F-keys of the panels █                  "
"                  ║   Everywhere          │   are mc's, in Normal and Visual mode and in quick       █                  "
"                  ║   Panels              │   search.                                                █                  "
"                  ║   Text fields         │ - Text fields open in Insert mode, where characters are  █                  "
"                  ║   Search and renaming │   text; Esc goes to Normal mode, and Esc there closes.   █                  "
"                  ║   Command line        │ - Quick search and the command line close on Esc, as     █                  "
"                  ║   Lists and menus     │   vim's search and command line do.                      █                  "
"                  ║   Menus and dialogs   │ - The line above the F-key bar says the mode, NORMAL,    ░                  "
"                  ║   Viewer              │   INSERT, or VISUAL, and the window that has the keys,   ░                  "
"                  ║   Tips                │   as INSERT · Quick search; (insert) is the one command  ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   of Normal mode after Ctrl+o. The cursor is a bar in    ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   Insert mode.                                           ░                  "
"                  ║                       │ - Alt and a key stand for Esc and the key in Insert and  ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   Visual mode and in the panels, but on a password, and  ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   in the dialogs and the pull-down menu, where Alt and a ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   highlighted letter act on what has it.                 ░                  "
"                  ║                       │ - Ctrl+c closes or cancels in every mode.                ░                  "
"                  ║                       │                                                          ░                  "
"                  ║                       │ ── Counts and registers ──────────────────────────────── ░                  "
"                  ║                       │ - In Normal mode, a count goes before a command: 5j goes ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   five rows down, 3G to the third row, 2g t to the       ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   second tab, and d3w deletes three words.               ░                  "
"                  ║                       │ - In text fields, "a names a register, which every field ░                  "
"                  ║                       │   shares, and A appends to it.                           ░                  "
"                  ║                       │                                                          ▼                  "
